    "body": "While the README highlights the focus on privacy the resulting application sadly doesn't. I don't think it's intended so I hope that the report helps to start investigating the reasons for that and remove the tracks from the Code:\r\n\r\nhttps://reports.exodus-privacy.eu.org/en/reports/69301/\r\n\r\nThe exodus report indicates that there are code signatures of 11 trackers/ad services involved. **Important: It doesn't mean they are active, but that's something that should be investigated**.\r\n\r\nMy idea where this comes from: Dependencies. Since I already mention I don't expect it to be intentional, there is likely that those trackers came as \"side-loaded content\" by one of the dependencies. Anyway, I think it's important to find and getting rid of them. Hope you get this fixed soon as the app is great! GPL :+1: ",
